  "title": "Garage & Exterior Stone Ideas | May 2025 GenStone Projects",
  "description": "Explore May 2025 GenStone garage and exterior facade projects. See curb appeal upgrades using easy DIY stone panels.",
  "canonicalUrl": "https://genstone.com/insights/project-spotlights/may-2025",
  "text": "GenStone Project Highlights – May 2025 Garage & Exterior Facade Projects\n\nAmanda Lombard\nDirector\n\nMay projects focused on exterior improvements, especially garage facades and front-of-home upgrades that improve curb appeal. These projects show how GenStone can quickly elevate the appearance of a home with targeted upgrades.\nTry Visualizer Get Project Planning Guide\n\n\"I'm a 76-year-old lady, and as the saying goes, \" did it myself.\" We LOVE the finished look...lots of compliments.\"\n\nCarol\n\nGarage Stone Projects\n\nExplore more garage stone ideas\n\nGarage areas are one of the most effective places to use GenStone because they are highly visible and often overlooked. This month featured projects where homeowners framed garage doors and added contrast to siding, creating a more finished and intentional exterior look.\n\n15\n\nChris’ Brick Veneer RV Garage\nIf you need to upgrade your RV garage, our Multi Color Brick Veneer is a great siding choice. Faux brick is the perfect DIY solution!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nMulti Color\n\nAlex Padilla\nProject Coordinator\n\n2\n\nDIY Faux Stone Garage Siding\nLooking for siding inspiration? Check out this DIY garage siding project that uses GenStone's Kenai faux stone for inspiration!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n5\n\nEric’s DIY Faux Stone Garage\nFaux stone is perfect for a home DIY project — whether the project is your garage or entry, stone veneer is the solution you need!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/MnJ4znjcuK9wieqxvCN4sM.jpg\" data-uuid=\"MnJ4znjcuK9wieqxvCN4sM\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/>\n\nMichael’s Faux Stone Garage And Entry\nOur faux stone is great at dressing up a home's garage and entry. Take a look at Michael's project for inspiration!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nStratford\n\n4\n\nDan’s Faux Slate Garage\nInstantly upgrade your curb appeal with a faux slate garage using GenStone's Vanilla Bean DIY-friendly panels.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nVanilla Bean\n\nSean McNamara\nProject Coordinator\n\n11\n\nChris’ Home and Garage Wainscoting\nUpdating your home and garage is easy with faux stone! This home and garage wainscoting project quickly and easily upgraded with faux stone.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n57\n\nDan’s Stone Veneer Garage Front\nThis customer opted for Keystone Stacked Stone to put stone veneer around his garage front to make it stand out and be more inviting.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKeystone\n\nExterior Facade Projects\n\nView more exterior stone ideas\n\nExterior facade upgrades can dramatically improve the look of a home without a full remodel. May projects included entryways, front elevations, and partial siding upgrades that added depth and architectural interest.\n\n<iframe title=\"MyGenStoneDIY - Kenai House by Dave\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/803178458?dnt=1&amp;app_id=122963\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\"></iframe> 8\n\nDave’s Faux Stone Home Siding Transformation\nThinking of transforming your siding? Check out this DIY home siding transformation that used our Kenai faux stone panels!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\nRyan Walsh\nProject Coordinator\n\n2\n\nDIY Exterior Home Renovation\nLooking to give your home an update? Check out this do it yourself Exterior Home Renovation using Keystone stacked stone panels by GenStone.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nStratford\n\n37\n\nDIY Faux Stone Home Siding\nIf you need to remodel your home siding and garden wall with an easy DIY project, look no further than GenStone's faux stone!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nDesert Sunrise\n\n4\n\nGregory’s Faux Stone Exterior Siding\nTransform your home's exterior siding with GenStone's faux stone. You can completely remodel your home on a budget. Take a look!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n2\n\nHunter’s Home Siding Ideas\nThe addition of faux stacked stone to the exterior of this home compliments the brick beautifully. Get ideas for your home.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nDesert Sunrise\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/mqH9kpxw8v83vKQg28H7U9.jpg\" data-uuid=\"mqH9kpxw8v83vKQg28H7U9\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 2957\n\nHow Earl Covered His Old Brick Wall\nYou can cover up an old brick wall with GenStone faux stone panels. Watch how Earl, a 79 year old weekend warrior covered up his old brick.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nDesert Sunrise\n\nJim’s Faux Stone Accent Siding\nYou can completely transform your home's exterior using GenStone's faux stone panels, like this project did with some accent siding. Take a look!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKeystone\n\n9\n\nKaren’s Home Siding Renovation\nThis customer undertook a huge DIY home siding renovation project with GenStone. See the before and after photos of this transformation!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nCoffee\n\nKenny’s DIY Home Siding Makeover\nIf you're looking for a DIY home siding makeover project, check out Kenny's! He used GenStone's stacked stone to transform his home exterior!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n12\n\nLakehouse Siding Project Idea\nUsing our Coffee Stacked Stone panels, this customer gave their lakehouse siding and wainscoting a significant upgrade.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/aVCXHdbzckc79TQP4VjRC2.jpg\" data-uuid=\"aVCXHdbzckc79TQP4VjRC2\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 2\n\nWilliam and Leslie’s Easy DIY Home Siding\nWant an easy DIY home siding project? Check out how easy it is to install GenStone's faux stone in this customer's video!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\nWhat Our Customers Are Saying\n\n“GenStone completely changed the look of the front of my house. It made a huge difference in curb appeal.”\n\n— Joel\n\n“I absolutely love the way GenStone looks on my house. It really upgraded the exterior.”\n\n— Lisa\n\n“The outside looks great and really improved the overall appearance of our home.”\n\n— Douglas\n\nFAQs\nAsk Away. We've Heard it All.\n\nAre GenStone panels weather resistant?\n\nYes. GenStone panels are designed to withstand outdoor conditions including rain, snow, and temperature changes, making them suitable for exterior projects.\n\nAmanda Lombard\n\nDirector\n\nCan GenStone be installed indoors and outdoors?\n\nYes. GenStone panels are designed for both interior and exterior applications. They are commonly used for accent walls, fireplace surrounds, entryways, garages, outdoor kitchens, and exterior facades.\n\nEvan Trevenna\n\nSenior Project Coordinator\n\nHow do I estimate how much GenStone I need for my project?\n\nYou can use the GenStone material calculator or contact a Project Coordinator for a full estimate. Most homeowners measure the square footage of the wall area and then account for corners, trim, and a small 5% waste factor.\n\nTravis Choate\n\nProject Coordinator\n\nDo GenStone panels require maintenance?\n\nGenStone requires very little maintenance. Most installations only need occasional cleaning with mild soap and water to remove dust or debris.\n\nJagger Gottschalk\n\nProject Coordinator\n\nTrending Upgrade Areas this Month\n\nAccent Wall Projects\n\nCreate a bold focal point in any room with lightweight stone panels that install quickly and add depth, texture, and warmth.\n\nView Projects\n\nChimney Projects\n\nUpgrade your chimney with realistic stone panels that add height, texture, and a finished look without the weight of masonry.\n\nView Projects\n\nPorch Projects\n\nTurn your porch into a stunning area with stacked stone panels that create a welcoming environment.\n\nView Projects",
